--
Unit proof for big-int ring identities (commutativity, additive inverse,
subtraction round-trip, int-agreement) over bounded nondeterministic
operands.  KNOWNBUG: the propositional reduction runs out of memory (16
GiB cap) -- BigInt's heap-allocated digit vectors blow up the formula.
Candidates to unblock: field-sensitive slicing, smaller digit type, or
SMT back-end.  Flip to CORE when it converges.

SMT BACK-ENDS 2026-07-17: --z3 (4.8.12) and --cvc5 (1.2.1) both get
past encoding easily (the SAT path OOMs at 14 GiB during propositional
reduction; SMT2 conversion is cheap) but neither SOLVES the formula:
z3 idle-loops >30 min, cvc5 >20 min (QF_AUFBV resp. ALL+FPA).  The
--cvc5 run initially failed on a CBMC SMT2-generation bug (unquoted
"::" in datatype selector names), fixed alongside this note.  So the
symbolic-size heap-array blow-up shifts from encoding memory (SAT) to
solve time (SMT); the harness-side fix (concrete digit capacities)
remains the promising route.
